  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Connect youth programme - Caritas Makeni</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Caritas Makeni is a national NGO instituted by the Bishop of Makeni in 1979. Since then it has been involved in development and relief operations in northern Sierra Leone. Generally, Caritas Makeni supports emergency and development projects in  peace building and reconciliation, child protection,  community capacity building, and rural infrastructure development.

Specific program interventions include:

?Mobilization of local communities, planning, implementation and management of project at local level.
?Providing technical assistance and support for projects implemented by grassroots groups.
?Supporting justice and peace development initiative and Programmes.
?Supporting relief inventions e.g. food aid.
?Supporting agricultural extension and small scale enterprise development.

The institution is committed to the human development of disadvantage, the structural transformation of the societies in which they live, and the enhancement of the physical environment upon which they depend for their survival. To effect change, the institution promotes a participatory growing process of integral development based on the formation of micro &#x2013; organizations among the disadvantaged to promote their own initiatives.
The project is about providing Caritas Makeni institutional core cost support while conducting baseline surveys for the development a strategic proposal for the implementation of their strategic plan.  It seeks to provide the organisational an opportunity to reorganise their organisation and management structures with a long term strategic plan. As an institutional core cost support project, it will enhance the finalization of CM&#x2019;s human resource management and  financial management for effective management. Part of this project support will go for beneficiaries and stakeholder awareness and needs assessment.</narrative>
  </description>
